To terminate a C program, you can use the exit() function from the stdlib.h library. This will cause your program to immediately stop executing and return control back to the operating system.

Here's an example of how to use it:

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main()
{
    printf("Hello World!\n");
    exit(0);
}

In this example, we first include the necessary libraries (stdio.h for input/output functions and stdlib.h for the exit() function). We then define our main() function where we print "Hello World!" using printf(). Finally, we call exit(0)
